# Demo — Minimal runnable pseudo-code (FastAPI + pseudo-LangChain style)

Below is an actionable skeleton you can paste into your repository and flesh out with your infra and LLM SDK.

```python
# pseudo-code, not a drop-in executable
from fastapi import FastAPI, Request
from pydantic import BaseModel

app = FastAPI()

class TaskRequest(BaseModel):
    requester: str
    goal: str
    contract_id: str = None

@app.post("/agents/contract-triage")
async def run_contract_agent(req: TaskRequest):
    run_id = start_run(req)
    # Planner: ask LLM to create plan
    plan = planner_create_plan(req.goal, req.contract_id)
    log(run_id, "plan", plan)

    for step in plan:
        if step["name"] == "fetch_contract":
            doc = secure_fetch(step["args"]["contract_id"], requester=req.requester)
            log(run_id, "fetch_contract", {"status":"ok","doc_id":doc.id})
        elif step["name"] == "extract_clause_summary":
            summary = llm_call_summarize(doc.text, step["args"]["clauses"])
            log(run_id, "clauses", summary)
        elif step["name"] == "risk_assessment":
            score = risk_model.score(summary)
            log(run_id,"risk_score", score)
        elif step["name"] == "generate_redlines":
            redlines = llm_generate_redlines(doc.text, constraints=policy_rules)
            log(run_id,"redlines", redlines)
        elif step["name"] == "create_jira" and score >= 0.5:
            issue = jira.create_issue(project="LEGAL", summary="Contract triage", description=compose_desc(summary, redlines))
            log(run_id,"jira",issue.key)
    finalize_run(run_id)
    return {"run_id": run_id, "jira": issue.key}
```

# The Build — Tools, technologies, and why

(Enterprise choices; pick cloud or on-prem variants)

Models

* Primary LLMs: Hosted enterprise LLM (OpenAI/Anthropic) + on-prem large models for sensitive data.
* Model management: versioning, A/B testing, model card metadata, regen seeds, cost tracking.

Data & Retrieval

* Vector DB: Milvus / Pinecone / Weaviate — for semantic search & embeddings.
* Indexer: ETL pipeline to parse PDFs, Office docs, emails; embeddings created with a stable embedder.
* Primary DB: Postgres for state + Redis for ephemeral context.

Orchestration & Compute

* Kubernetes (EKS/GKE/AKS) or serverless containers — autoscaling.
* Worker queue: Kafka / RabbitMQ / Google Pub/Sub for high throughput.

Tooling & Connectors

* Connector adapters: Jira, Salesforce, Slack, ServiceNow, SAP, internal REST/gRPC APIs.
* Sandbox for running code, SQL queries or scripts: restrictive container runtime with resource limits and ACLs.

Security & Governance

* Identity: SAML/OIDC + SCIM for provisioning (Okta, Azure AD).
* Secrets: Vault / Cloud KMS.
* Data protection: Tokenization & PII redaction; policies for not sending PII to third-party LLMs unless allowed.
* Policy Engine: Declarative rules for approvals, e.g., “if contract risk > 0.5 then require legal approval”.

Observability & Testing

* Tracing: Jaeger.
* Metrics: Prometheus + Grafana dashboards.
* Logs & audit: Elasticsearch / Splunk.
* Unit & integration testing: pytest; contract tests for tool adapters.
* Canary & chaos testing for resilience.

DevOps

* CI/CD: GitHub Actions / GitLab CI to build images, run security scans, run integration tests.
* Helm charts + Kustomize for manifests.
* IaC: Terraform for infra.

Compliance

* Immutable audit logs, data residency options, configurable data retention, customer isolation (multi-tenant vs single-tenant).

# Safety, governance & explainability

* Decision trace for every agent-run (plan, prompts, tools invoked, model versions, redactions).
* Human-in-the-loop gates for high-risk actions (financial > $X, contractual risk > Y).
* Prompt & output sanitizers, regex redactors for secrets.
* Policy engine enforces “do-not-send” lists and jurisdictional rules (GDPR/PIPEDA).
* Explainability: LLM produces short rationale with each critical decision (1–2 sentences).

# Metrics & KPIs

Track:

* Task success rate (automated completion without human handover).
* Time-to-resolution (minutes/hours saved).
* Mean time to recovery (for incident workflows).
* Precision of extraction (NLP F1 vs human gold).
* False positives/negatives for risk scoring.
* Cost per run (LLM tokens + infra).

# Deployment checklist — MVP to Prod

MVP (4–8 weeks)

* Basic planner + retriever + 3 tool adapters (Jira, Slack, Document store).
* Vector DB with synced contract docs.
* LLM integration (enterprise API).
* Basic UI to trigger runs + view traces.
* Simple policy: create_jira if risk > 0.5.

Production (2–3 months)

* SSO integration + RBAC.
* Secrets manager + data encryption.
* Observability + alerts.
* Hardening: rate limits, quotas, circuit breakers for LLM provider.
* Testing harness + load tests.

Enterprise scale (3–6 months)

* Multi-region deployment and DR.
* On-prem model hosting for sensitive workloads.
* Fine-grained data governance and customer isolation.
* MLOps for model retraining, evaluation, and drift detection.

